---
# Copyright © 2026 Zenin Easa Panthakkalakath
#
# Scoped to the checks most relevant to a memory-safety pass: use-after-free/dangling-pointer
# patterns (bugprone-*), raw-owning-pointer misuse (cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory), and unsafe
# type-punning/casts (cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-*). Deliberately not a broader "everything"
# config yet -- see docs on this repo's memory-safety pass for why: a first run needs triaging
# before more check families are worth turning on, and a huge default check set would mostly
# flag pre-existing, already-reviewed style choices rather than real defects.
#
# First full triage (43 findings) is done: 2 were real bugs (fixed -- both main()s now wrap their
# whole body in a try/catch, not just the dispatch logic), a handful of small numeric-cast issues
# were fixed directly, and a handful of genuinely rare cases got a targeted NOLINT with a reason
# (see providerInProcessShim.cpp, providerRuntime.cpp, modelValidator.cpp). The three casting
# checks below are disabled category-wide rather than suppressed line-by-line: every one of their
# 25 combined hits was a legitimate, structurally necessary use (binary-protocol byte headers,
# OpenSSL/zlib C-API const-correctness gaps, POSIX exec/shm/sem calls, dlopen) -- this engine's
# nature as a binary-protocol/C-ABI-provider layer makes them pervasive and expected here, not
# incidental, so the check doesn't earn its keep in this codebase the way it would in
# higher-level C++ that shouldn't need raw casts or varargs at all.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-cstyle-cast,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-static-cast-downcast,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-union-access,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '^.*/engine/(include|src)/.*'
FormatStyle: none
